# Bot1's Ornithopter attacks unblocked; in the declare blockers step Bot1 casts Splinter's Technique for {1}{B} (Mox Jet and
# Mox Ruby, the pool left empty), returning the Ornithopter to hand. As a sorcery it enters nothing: it searches the library for
# Black Lotus, which goes to the hand, then shuffles, and is put in the graveyard. Its text says "put that card into your hand", not
# "reveal", so no card is revealed (Revealed is absent for both players). Bot2's library is not searched.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Ornithopter
Splinter's Technique
Swamp x6
Black Lotus
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Black Lotus
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot1.Hand.Splinter's Technique.Cast(Ability: Sneak)
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Search(Black Lotus)
? Bot1.Revealed = (absent)
? Bot2.Revealed = (absent)
? Bot1.Mana =
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Ruby
Bot1.Hand = Black Lotus; Ornithopter; Swamp; Swamp; Swamp; Swamp
Bot1.Graveyard = Splinter's Technique
Bot2.Library.Count = 12
